==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 6.67~16.67 seconds<sup>200f~500f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Heavenly Hippoe]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 23.33~33.33 seconds<sup>700f~1,000f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Divine Cyclone]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Angel Fanboy]] spawns.
**3 [[Gabriel]]s spawn, delay 0.67~1.33 seconds<sup>20f~40f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn, delay 13.33~23.33 seconds<sup>400f~700f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Due to Divine Cyclone's extremely high DPS and lack of knockbacks, the use of Anti-Angel Units with slow, freeze, or knockback abilities is mandatory. Talented [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] trivializes this stage. If you don't have their talents, then you must rely on [[Stilts Cat (Rare Cat)|Stilts Cat]] or the 2 [[Juliet Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Super]] [[Cat Toaster (Super Rare Cat)|Rares]] that target Angels instead.

[[Ancient Heroes ULTRA SOULS (Gacha Event)|ULTRA SOULS]] Ubers in their first form are very helpful in this stage, as their anti-Angel abilities will either help kill the Cyclone faster (e.g. [[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasa Jizo]], [[Issun Boshi (Uber Rare Cat)|Issun Boshi]], [[Ushiwakamaru (Legend Rare Cat)|Ushiwakamaru]]) or, especially if you don't have talented Sanzo Cat, serve as powerful crowd-controllers (e.g. [[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|The Grateful Crane]], [[Princess Kaguya (Uber Rare Cat)|Princess Kaguya]], [[Momotaro (Uber Rare Cat)|Momotaro]]).

==Trivia==
*Oncoming Maelstrom was the first level added to the game to contain Angel enemies.

